        <templateparamlist>
          <param>
            <type>typename T</type>
          </param>
        </templateparamlist>
        <type>std::pair&lt; Math::Tensors::FastorTensors::Tensor33t&lt; T &gt;, Math::Tensors::FastorTensors::Tensor3333t&lt; T &gt; &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::pair&lt; Math::Tensors::FastorTensors::Tensor33t&lt; T &gt;, Math::Tensors::FastorTensors::Tensor3333t&lt; T &gt; &gt; Marmot::ContinuumMechanics::Kinematics::DeformationMeasures::FirstOrder::rightCauchyGreen</definition>
        <argsstring>(const Math::Tensors::FastorTensors::Tensor33t&lt; T &gt; &amp;F)</argsstring>
        <name>rightCauchyGreen</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::ContinuumMechanics::Kinematics::DeformationMeasures::FirstOrder::rightCauchyGreen</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const Math::Tensors::FastorTensors::Tensor33t&lt; T &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>F</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Computes the right Cauchy-Green tensor <formula id="5">$\boldsymbol{C}$</formula> and its derivative with respect to <formula id="1">$\boldsymbol{F}$</formula>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Scalar type (e.g., float, double, autodiff::dual) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>F</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Deformation gradient tensor </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A pair containing the right Cauchy-Green tensor C and its derivative with respect to F</para>
</simplesect>
The right Cauchy-Green deformation tensor is defined as:   <formula id="6">\[  \boldsymbol{C} = \boldsymbol{F}^T \boldsymbol{F}
\]</formula> or in index notation:   <formula id="7">\[  C_{IJ} = F_{iI} F_{iJ}
\]</formula> The derivative of <formula id="5">$\boldsymbol{C}$</formula> with respect to <formula id="1">$\boldsymbol{F}$</formula> is given by:   <formula id="11">\[ \frac{\partial C_{IJ}}{\partial F_{kK}} = \delta_{IK} F_{kJ} + F_{kI} \delta_{JK}
\]</formula> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
